ided by going river left.","caption":"Above the undercut wall","poi_name":"undercut wall","subject":"","author":"Kemper Begley","poi_id":"102985","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878609","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878609"}},{"id":"878611","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879051","description":"Marlo Wright paddles through the best rapid on White's Creek.","caption":"Signature rapid of White's Creek","poi_name":"White's Creek","subject":"Marlo Wright","author":"Kemper Begley","poi_id":"102989","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878611","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878611"}},{"id":"878613","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879053","description":"Paul Butler runs the rapid beside the undercut wall. White's Creek is beautiful in October.","caption":"Fall scenery on White's Creek","poi_name":"undercut wall","subject":"Paul Butler","author":"Kemper Begley","poi_id":"102985","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878613","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878613"}},{"id":"878614","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879054","description":"Paul Butler paddles past the two holes at Surf City. There is good play here if you're in the mood.","caption":"the two play holes at Surf City","poi_name":"Surf City","subject":"Paul Butler","author":"Kemper Begley","poi_id":"102988","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878614","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878614"}},{"id":"883604","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"886296","description":"Watch out for the undercut left of rock.","caption":"Butcher's Block","poi_name":"Butcher's Block","subject":"","author":"Simon K","poi_id":"102985","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883604","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883604"}},{"id":"883606","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"886298","description":"Everyones favorit rapid on this section of Whites Creek.\r\n","caption":"Danger Will Robinson","poi_name":"Danger Will Robinson","subject":"","author":"Simon","poi_id":"102984","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883606","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883606"}},{"id":"883607","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"886300","description":"George and Debbi rockin Swat Spot","caption":"Swat Spot","poi_name":"Swat Spot","subject":"","author":"Simon","poi_id":"102989","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883607","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883607"}},{"id":"883608","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"886301","description":"A good amount of maneuver's @ 1.5 feet before slamming into the large cliff wall on rivers right with a dangerous undercut.  At low water this is a good rapid to scout.","caption":"Simple Simon","poi_name":"Simple Simon","subject":"","author":"Simon","poi_id":"102988","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883608","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883608"}}],"detail":{"id":"1799","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"See also [Upper White's Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/3111/).\n\nJust before you get to Butcher Block (so within the first half mile of the run) there is a hazardous pin rock in the right line of an otherwise non-descript smaller rapid. Level was around 1.1 feet on the take-out gauge. It probably doesn't take a lot more water than that to put it completely underwater. We got a boat badly pinned there, requiring a 3:1 z-drag to remove. Stay left of center to avoid.\n\n(Note: there is an emergency walkout road to the put-in just below this rock on river left. We didn't have to use it, but you can see where it is.)\n\n**River Description:**\n\nClay Wright 2004-02-06 22:33:58 3.5 to 4.5' great play on the lower.\n\nAfter a few good waves you get to the first river-wide hole. Eddy both sides - it's excellent for all tricks- even loops.\n\nThere is one hole on a right bend shortly below the surf spot which feeds into a left eddy backed by a rock and wall, and it comes up fast. Left to right cut required, or out the back of the eddy.\n\nThe 'undercut right wall' is easy to go left of if you see it coming in advance - stay left each time you see big cliff on river right and you'll breeze it.\n\nSeveral flooded islands make it hard to find the river-bad. We often found clean channels far right.\n\nBest front-surfing just below confluence with a big creek on left. You'll want to walk back up again and again - a camp on the right makes it possible (kinda long).\n\nCouple more tree-lined mazes (one far right, and go L at the RR bridge) and you're done. < br /> Clay Wright\n\nEmory at Obed went from 14g to 53g; Daddy's up to 8g,","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"5.5","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109267","114506","102984","102988","102989"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-84.81191,35.796815],[-84.811851,35.796878],[-84.811755,35.796998],[-84.811714,35.797061],[-84.811643,35.797152],[-84.811463,35.797396],[-84.81139,35.797485],[-84.81136,35.797512],[-84.811234,35.79761],[-84.811129,35.797676],[-84.811062,35.797722],[-84.81099,35.797763],[-84.810912,35.797798],[-84.810791,35.79784],[-84.810749,35.79785],[-84.810662,35.797865],[-84.810443,35.797895],[-84.809964,35.797931],[-84.809878,35.79793],[-84.809684,35.797944],[-84.809511,35.79795],[-84.809381,35.79796],[-84.809251,35.797965],[-84.808854,35.797962],[-84.808677,35.797965],[-84.807968,35.797